<!--
  MachineBlocks — MBML documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml.TypeSystem
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbml="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml"
  xmlns:mbt="com.machineblocks.bml.type"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <name>TypeSystem</name>
  <type>mbml:TypeSystem</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks domain types</is>

  <documentation>
    MachineBlocks domain ValueTypes live in com.machineblocks.bml.type.*. They are the SSOT for
    type shapes used by NativeBlock properties and other domain members. Do not redefine types from
    Markdown or YAML.

    Categories (illustrative — see package members for the full inventory):

    Atomic enums — Axis, Face, Direction, Align, StudType, HoleType, Gender, and related.
    Axis containers — AxisXY(T), AxisXYZ(T), AxisAB(T) for per-axis values.
    Face / side maps — FaceMapXY, FaceMapXYZ, CornerMap, Per-side and hole-edge maps.
    Size and offset — SizeXYZ, SizeXY, SizeAB, OffsetXYZ, OffsetXY, OffsetAB, RotationXYZ.
    Domain compounds — Connector, ScrewHole, WallGap / RecessWallGap, Port, Grille, SelectiveGrid,
      rounding maps, quality profiles, PCB types.

    Naming uses XYZ / XY / AB axis keys — not 3D / 2D labels.

    MBOM values are canonical. Render targets serialize those values (for SCAD mappings see the
    SCAD TypesAndSerialization documentation). NativeBlock property type attributes reference these
    types directly.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="mbml:AuthoringPatterns" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — MBML authoring patterns for simple and composite blocks.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:SizeXYZ" relation="SeeAlso">
      Example compound type — integer grid size.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:SelectiveGrid" relation="SeeAlso">
      Example generic grid selector used by studs and related features.
    </see>
    <see type="mbt:Connector" relation="SeeAlso">
      Example domain compound for discrete connectors.
    </see>
    <see type="scad:TypesAndSerialization" relation="SeeAlso">
      MBOM → SCAD serialization of these types.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/04_types.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      BlockML / MBOM type naming and conventions.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
